<title>USA: US to sell $27 bln 2-,5-yr notes July 22,23.</title>
<headline>US to sell $27 bln 2-,5-yr notes July 22,23.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Treasury Department said on Wednesday that it will sell $15.5 billion of 2-year notes on July 22 and $11.5 bln of 5-yr notes on July 23 to refund $30.369 billion of securities maturing July 31 and to pay down about $3.375 billion.</p>
<p>The notes will be issued on July 31. The two-year notes mature on July 31, 1999 and the five-year notes mature on July 31, 2002.</p>
<p>The CUSIP number for the 2-year notes will be 9128273B6 and for the five-year notes will be 9128273C4.</p>
</text>
